{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 491259, "name": "Adam Williamson", "username": "adamwill", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/adamwill/{size}/377_2.png", "created_at": "2026-04-08T17:38:55.678Z", "cooked": "<p>The Quality team has orphaned these packages:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>python-aniso8601</li>\n<li>python-flask-caching</li>\n<li>testcloud</li>\n<li>python-pytest-xprocess</li>\n<li>python-flask-restful</li>\n</ul>\n<p>See <a href=\"https://forge.fedoraproject.org/quality/tickets/issues/880\">team ticket discussing this</a>. This is part of the <a href=\"https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/fedora-quality-scope-reduction-announcement-and-summary/160523\">effort by the portion of the team employed by Red Hat to reduce our responsibilities</a> since our headcount was reduced last year.</p>\n<p>These are the things that would be impacted by the packages being retired, if that were to happen. .src dependencies are packages that would fail to <em>build</em> without the orphaned packages. arched dependencies are packages that would fail to <em>install</em> without the orphaned packages.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">Dependencies of other packages that would be BROKEN by the specified source package removals:\npackage: conda-25.11.1-3.fc44.src from https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/fedora/linux/development/44/Everything/source/tree/\n  python3-pytest-xprocess\npackage: copr-frontend-2.6.hotfix.4-1.fc44.noarch from https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/fedora/linux/development/44/Everything/x86_64/os/\n  python3dist(flask-caching)\npackage: copr-frontend-2.6.hotfix.4-1.fc44.src from https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/fedora/linux/development/44/Everything/source/tree/\n  python3dist(flask-caching)\npackage: python-cachelib-0.13.0-10.fc44.src from https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/fedora/linux/development/44/Everything/source/tree/\n  python3-pytest-xprocess\npackage: python-flask-compress-1.23-2.fc44.src from https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/fedora/linux/development/44/Everything/source/tree/\n  python3dist(flask-caching)\npackage: python-flask-restx-1.3.0-12.fc44.src from https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/fedora/linux/development/44/Everything/source/tree/\n  python3dist(aniso8601) &gt;= 0.82\npackage: python3-flask-restx-1.3.0-12.fc44.noarch from https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/fedora/linux/development/44/Everything/x86_64/os/\n  python3.14dist(aniso8601) &gt;= 0.82\n</code></pre>\n<p>We expect the Fedora CI team will likely pick up testcloud, since they now own it upstream. Python folks might be interested in picking up some or all of the others.</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 1, "updated_at": "2026-04-08T17:39:14.462Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 6, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 34.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 185856, "topic_slug": "orphaned-packages-python-aniso8601-python-flask-caching-testcloud-python-pytest-xprocess-python-flask-restful", "display_username": "Adam Williamson", "primary_group_name": "qa", "flair_name": "qa", "flair_url": "bug", "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 77, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/fedora-quality-scope-reduction-announcement-and-summary/160523", "internal": true, "reflection": false, "title": "Fedora Quality scope reduction announcement and summary", "clicks": 2}, {"url": "https://forge.fedoraproject.org/quality/tickets/issues/880", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Making sure you're not a bot!", "clicks": 1}], "read": true, "user_title": "Packaging Team", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 387, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 2, "deleted_at": null, "user_d